Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 03:20:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Vietnamese default Accept-Language: drop French (vi,en-US,en)

On a fresh Vietnamese profile, chrome://settings languages and the
intl.accept_languages pref defaulted to Vietnamese, French, English
(US), English. The French entry is seeded entirely by the vi
translation of IDS_ACCEPT_LANGUAGES (the HTTP Accept-Language default),
which upstream Chromium ships as "vi-VN,vi,fr-FR,fr,en-US,en" in
components/strings/components_locale_settings_vi.xtb -- a historical
Google-translations artifact, not anything colorburst added.

Drop the fr-FR,fr pair so the colorburst default is Vietnamese, English
(US), English, matching a de-Googled Vietnamese target audience that
does not want French preloaded.

---
 components/strings/components_locale_settings_vi.xtb | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/components/strings/components_locale_settings_vi.xtb b/components/strings/components_locale_settings_vi.xtb
index c5a5db3db1..dc7febcd72 100644
--- a/components/strings/components_locale_settings_vi.xtb
+++ b/components/strings/components_locale_settings_vi.xtb
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 <?xml version="1.0" ?>
 <!DOCTYPE translationbundle>
 <translationbundle lang="vi">
-<translation id="IDS_ACCEPT_LANGUAGES">vi-VN,vi,fr-FR,fr,en-US,en</translation>
+<translation id="IDS_ACCEPT_LANGUAGES">vi-VN,vi,en-US,en</translation>
 <translation id="IDS_DEFAULT_ENCODING">windows-1258</translation>
 </translationbundle>
